---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { proseClass } from './_seo';
---
<Base pageType="policy" title="About the SizeTune image resizer | SizeTune" description="SizeTune is a free browser tool that resizes photos and signatures to a size in KB. Read why it exists, how it works, its limits, and who runs it." path="/about/">
  <h1 class="mb-3 text-3xl font-bold">About SizeTune</h1>
  <div class={proseClass}>
    <h2>What it is</h2>
    <p>
      SizeTune is a small, free website that reduces an image to fit a file size limit. It was made for the common
      moment when a form rejects a photo or signature because it is a few KB too large. It is independent and is not
      connected to any government body, exam board, employer or application portal.
    </p>

    <h2>How it works</h2>
    <p>
      The tool runs in your browser. It searches for the best balance of picture quality and pixel dimensions that
      keeps the file under your limit, and it reports honestly when a limit cannot be met. The
      <a href="/privacy/">privacy page</a> explains what that means for your images, and the
      <a href="/guides/photo-size-for-online-forms/">photo size guide</a> explains the ideas behind it.
    </p>

    <h2>What we try to do, and what we do not claim</h2>
    <p>
      We write guidance from how the tool actually behaves and say so when a statement depends on your device or
      browser. We do not promise a particular result, we do not publish rules for specific forms because those change,
      and we ask you to follow the instructions on your own form. Pages show the date they were last updated.
    </p>

    <h2>Who runs it</h2>
    <p>
      SizeTune is run by [[HUMAN: owner name or pseudonym to show publicly, plus one sentence on who they are]].
      You can contact us at [[HUMAN: public contact email address]]. Please include the page address and your browser
      and device if you are reporting a problem. We read corrections to the guides and fix what we can verify.
    </p>
    <p>
      The terms for using the site are on the <a href="/terms/">terms page</a>. To try the tool, go to the
      <a href="/">home page</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
